  "changes": [
    "The existing primitive thresholds and their vendored desk twin remain byte/AST compatible. A new shared pure layer fixes the applicable feature denominator: incomplete inputs cannot inflate the weighted maximum/mean composite by dropping dimensions. Required/observed/missing and inapplicable features, borrowed baseline cohort, exact maximum/mean and formula are retained per row.",
    "All supplied measured auctions remain in the scoring population, including missing BTC, unknown identity and unsupported FRNs. Unsupported or incomplete positive-weight rows withhold the entire weighted window. No complete-case renormalization or favorable unsupported-instrument exclusion is introduced. Known zero amount has zero weight; no source row is deleted.",
    "Short-bill floor applicability requires known policy context. A missing rate or required discount-rate quote is unavailable; policy at or below one percent explicitly makes the floor inapplicable. Existing detector current-vintage policy context is unchanged. Desk history uses its already-acquired most recent prior DFF value only within five calendar days; missing policy no longer defaults to zero.",
    "Both native detector and native desk history call the same completeness compiler and once-rounded per-auction score. Missing-BTC and unscorable rows remain in the historical denominator. The desk retains the existing current detector input separately as detector_context; it cannot overwrite and conceal an incomplete reconstructed window.",
    "Tenor maximums tolerate explicit nulls and withhold an incomplete bucket maximum. Zero indicator observations remain distinct from missing and inapplicable. Aggregates retain all applicable observations and coverage, separate counts at fifty and seventy, and explain incomplete counts as lower bounds. Seventy-point triggers no longer report fifty-point counts, and null current state cannot crash or become zero.",
    "Historical comparison cannot promote an incomplete current vector into zero coordinates or an arbitrary first-ranked anchor. Candidate anchors remain in all_matches with unavailable similarity; no top match is shown. This is a completeness guard only; the incompatible legacy anchor catalog/model remains unqualified and awaits separate repair.",
    "The public packet adds the complete auction_observations population and explicit counts while retaining recent_auctions as the legacy ten-row sample. Empty refresh clears the added population and counts. The page presents all acquired rows, count/scope and score-input disclosures, marks partial indicator coverage, and keeps measured zero separate from missing scores. Keyboard disclosure, bounded trace scrolling and contained horizontal mobile tables were visually checked."
  ],
