  "limitations": [
    "Fixed legacy thresholds, borrowed bill/short-coupon baselines, issuance overlay and historical anchor mappings remain uncalibrated. Complete arithmetic and source-row retention do not validate predictive edge or portfolio sizing.",
    "Current-vintage reconstruction and present-context detector scores do not establish historical availability. Desk history retains original sample cadence and legacy issuance overlay, while detector daily history still excludes that overlay; these are explicitly separate calculations.",
    "An unsupported positive-weight instrument can intentionally make the complete-population composite unavailable. It must not silently disappear merely to keep a number on the page.",
    "Full row input traces are not a newly frozen whole-model original-provider replay archive. Earlier Treasury/FRED archives remain separately bounded, with ordinary publication still pending the original 13:05 UTC schedule.",
    "No provider query, native invocation, cadence change, private/learning-ledger/downstream read, paid AI or resource expansion is introduced. All ten platform acceptance workstreams remain open."
  ],
